  "id": "COMPOUND:31329 - PROTEIN:5845",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between N2-Acetyl-L-Lysine and SNU1 through a series of intermediate targets. N2-Acetyl-L-Lysine is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Pronuciferine, Vitetrifolin B, and Diethylene glycol monolaurate, all of which have been shown to target Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates that N2-Acetyl-L-Lysine may act as a modulator or activator of Phosphodiesterase 6C, which in turn influences the activity of SNU1. The shared target of these compounds at Phosphodiesterase 6C suggests a possible mechanism by which N2-Acetyl-L-Lysine could interact with SNU1, potentially through the regulation of downstream signaling pathways. The consistent presence of SNU1 as a target across different compounds supports the hypothesis that N2-Acetyl-L-Lysine may exert its effects via Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
